{"id": "EUVD-2026-96902", "enisaUuid": "eafd54e9-a26a-33dd-85ed-7ccf2d1b5558", "description": "Speedtest Tracker through 1.15.0 contains an IP allowlist bypass vulnerability that allows unauthenticated remote attackers to evade ALLOWED_IPS and Prometheus allowlists by spoofing X-Forwarded-For headers. Because bootstrap/app.php trusts every peer as a proxy, attackers can supply an allowlisted address to read /prometheus metrics and reach protected web and API endpoints.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T12:19:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T17:00:42", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind03/speedtest-tracker-trust-proxies-allowlist-bypass", "https://github.com/alexjustesen/speedtest-tracker/blob/fce6eb36181ed70b5b0763c391a50b806d7e3da7/bootstrap/app.php#L23-L41", "https://github.com/alexjustesen/speedtest-tracker/blob/fce6eb36181ed70b5b0763c391a50b806d7e3da7/app/Http/Middleware/AllowedIpAddressesMiddleware.php#L16-L27", "https://github.com/alexjustesen/speedtest-tracker/blob/fce6eb36181ed70b5b0763c391a50b806d7e3da7/app/Http/Middleware/PrometheusAllowedIpMiddleware.php#L22-L42", "https://github.com/alexjustesen/speedtest-tracker", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/speedtest-tracker-through-1.15.0-ip-allowlist-bypass-via-x-forwarded-for-spoofing"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5mh8-m8gg-2f9w", "CVE-2026-108736"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "546a0bf0-6011-3c9d-ba4b-e6bd57ae9b56", "product": {"name": "speedtest-tracker", "vendor": {"name": "alexjustesen"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.15.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8429e701-c06d-3dac-bd51-0ab4124cbb90", "vendor": {"name": "alexjustesen"}}], "isExploited": false}